From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:37:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] hwui: Keep bigger Vulkan pipeline caches and stop resaving
 ones that don't fit

With skiavk the whole VkPipelineCache is stored as a single value, and on
Adreno it outgrows the 2MB value limit in apps with many pipelines. The
store is then refused, but mTryToStorePipelineCache stays set, so every
flushed frame serializes the full cache again only to have it thrown
away: hundreds of "sizes 4 2103842 not allowed" in a few seconds and a
busy RenderThread, and the pipelines are compiled again on every launch.

Allow 4MB values in an 8MB cache, and when a pipeline cache store is
refused, stop trying until new shaders are compiled.
---
 libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/ShaderCache.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/ShaderCache.cpp b/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/ShaderCache.cpp
index 22f59a6..0d14868 100644
--- a/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/ShaderCache.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/pipeline/skia/ShaderCache.cpp
@@ -36,8 +36,8 @@ namespace skiapipeline {
 
 // Cache size limits.
 static const size_t maxKeySize = 1024;
-static const size_t maxValueSize = 2 * 1024 * 1024;
-static const size_t maxTotalSize = 4 * 1024 * 1024;
+static const size_t maxValueSize = 4 * 1024 * 1024;
+static const size_t maxTotalSize = 8 * 1024 * 1024;
 static_assert(maxKeySize + maxValueSize < maxTotalSize);
 
 ShaderCache::ShaderCache() {
@@ -201,6 +201,9 @@ void ShaderCache::store(const SkData& key, const SkData& data, const SkString& /
     size_t keySize = key.size();
     if (keySize == 0 || valueSize == 0 || valueSize >= maxValueSize) {
         ALOGW("ShaderCache::store: sizes %d %d not allowed", (int)keySize, (int)valueSize);
+        if (mInStoreVkPipelineInProgress) {
+            mTryToStorePipelineCache = false;
+        }
         return;
     }
 
